Z||000000||fotofrank||05-07-2001||11:07 PM||||Will roller rockers do any good in an Iron Duke? What shoul I use and why? The object of my work is to increse torque. I have brought the Duke to about 104+ horse power and some added torque would be great. I'd get off the line quicker and get the "pushed in the seat" feeling.<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://www.homestead.com/fotofrank/foto1.html||||reg||5
Z||000001||erikred||05-08-2001||01:23 PM||||On a low reving mild engine I do not think you could notice the difference. I am not sure how they effect torque. It probably would not be worth the cost. It you want to check them out PAW list them for the Duke for $173.95 in my new catalog. They are manufactured by Crane and are aluminum w/ needle bearings. You could also buy ones made for a BBC.||||reg||1
